      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): preserve streamed assistant text when Claude CLI result event is empty",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nClaude CLI can stream a complete assistant answer and then emit an empty successful terminal result. OpenClaw previously treated that terminal envelope as authoritative, discarded the streamed answer, and failed the turn as an empty response.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nBoth JSONL consumers now preserve their already-accumulated assistant text only when the terminal result is successful and empty. Reusable Claude sessions finish from the same incremental parser that classified pre-tool commentary, so an empty terminal result cannot merge commentary back into the final answer. Non-empty terminal results and structured errors keep precedence, while a genuinely empty turn remains empty and follows the existing failover policy.\n\nThe original PR was rewritten on current `main`: the unused tool-call state and runner-policy tests were removed, leaving the parser-owned fix and focused regressions for the incremental and completed-transcript paths.\n\n## User Impact\n\nClaude CLI replies that fully arrive through streaming are no longer lost merely because the final result envelope is empty. Genuine empty turns still fail as before.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Exact head: `9ea40bb01ce7ad17d8485b8c89816681016a1fb0`\n- Sanitized AWS Crabbox: `cbx_a55917e324f7` (`crimson-krill`), public network, no instance role, no Tailscale, no hydration, exact-SHA bootstrap.\n- Focused tests: run `run_fcc27265a454`, `pnpm test src/agents/cli-output.test.ts src/agents/cli-runner.spawn.test.ts` — 135/135 passed. This includes reusable-live-session coverage proving pre-tool commentary remains commentary while the streamed final answer survives an empty result.\n- Source-blind CLI contract through `openclaw agent --local --json` and a deterministic Claude-style JSONL backend:\n  - streamed `first streamed answer`, then empty result → exit 0 with exact first text;\n  - streamed `second distinct answer`, then empty result → exit 0 with exact second text and no stale first text;\n  - no streamed text, then empty result → exit 1 with `CLI backend returned an empty response`.\n- Source-blind proof run: `run_4920491ee522`.\n- Fresh exact-head autoreview: clean, no accepted/actionable findings, confidence 0.86.\n- `git diff --check` passed; targeted `oxfmt` completed before commit.\n\nThe contributor's production Ubuntu proof remains useful before/after evidence for the intermittent real Claude CLI event sequence. The maintainer proof above revalidates the rewritten exact head through the user-facing local-agent command without credentials.\n",
        "branch": "fix/claude-cli-empty-result-preserve-streamed-text",
